a.cc`, `crypto/fipsmodule/{digest/digests.cc.inc,keccak/*}`, `include/openssl/{digest,nid}.h`","+- **SHA3-224, and NIDs + name lookup for upstream's SHA3-256/384/512 `EVP_MD`s** — `crypto/evp/p_keccak.cc`, `crypto/digest/digest_extra.cc`, `crypto/fipsmodule/keccak/*`, `include/openssl/{digest,nid}.h`"," - **HMAC-SHA3** — `crypto/hmac/hmac_test*.{cc,txt}`"," - **BLAKE2b-512** — `crypto/blake2/blake2.cc`, `include/openssl/blake2.h`"," - **RIPEMD160 in `crypto/` (not `decrepit/`) + `EVP_ripemd160` lookup** — `crypto/ripemd/ripemd.cc` (moved), `crypto/digest/digest_extra.cc`, `include/openssl/digest.h`, `gen/sources.*`, `build.json`","@@ -91,6 +91,11 @@ Then `bun run ci:watch` and fix anything that turns up."," - **Electron `SSL_want` / `EVP_CIPHER_do_all_sorted`** — `ssl/ssl_lib.cc` (return `rwstate` directly), `ssl/ssl_test.cc` (drops the corresponding test block), `decrepit/evp/evp_do_all.cc`, `crypto/cipher/get_cipher.cc`, `include/openssl/cipher.h`"," - **MLDSA stack-frame pragma** — `crypto/fipsmodule/mldsa/mldsa.cc.inc`"," - **PKCS#1 v1.5 signature prefixes for the digests above** — `crypto/fipsmodule/rsa/rsa.cc.inc` (`kPKCS1SigPrefixes` rows for SHA-512/224, SHA-512/256, SHA3-\\* and RIPEMD-160), `crypto/rsa/rsa_test.cc`","+- **`BORINGSSL_REQUIRE_MEMORY_HOOKS` / `OPENSSL_system_*`** — `crypto/{mem.cc,internal.h,err/err.cc,thread_*.cc}`, `ssl/ssl_buffer.cc`","+- **`BORINGSSL_PEM_FAST_PUBLIC_BASE64`** — `crypto/pem/pem_lib.cc`, `include/openssl/pem.h`","+- **`X509_LAZY_CERT_SET`, `X509_V_FLAG_IGNORE_EXPIRED_TRUST_ANCHORS`** — `crypto/x509/{x509_lu,x509_vfy,x_name}.cc`, `include/openssl/x509.h`","+- **`X509_V_ERR_UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE`** (upstream no longer reports it; Node does) — `check_lone_untrusted_leaf` in `crypto/x509/x509_vfy.cc`","+- **OpenSSL's verdicts in the path builder** (attribute-certificate CRLs, revocation of trust anchors, partial chains, `keyUsage`-only anchors, auto-chaining) — `crypto/x509/{x509_vfy,v3_purp}.cc`, `ssl/ssl_x509.cc`"," "," If upstream upstreams any of these (check `git grep` on `upstream/main` before re-applying), drop the fork's copy."," ","@@ -100,3 +105,4 @@ If upstream upstreams any of these (check `git grep` on `upstream/main` before r"," - **`BIO_read`/`BIO_write` error-value narrowing** — can change `SSL_read` error paths over memory BIOs (`SSLWrapper` for TLS-over-duplex). If `node-tls-connect.test.ts` crashes in `flush_pending_events`, see `src/runtime/socket/UpgradedDuplex.rs::teardown` and `WindowsNamedPipe.rs`'s `WRAPPER_BUSY` for the re-entrant-drop guard."," - **Per-handshake allocation churn (PQ key shares)** grows under ASAN quarantine; RSS-delta tests like `tls-connect-socket-churn.test.ts` may need their `isASAN` bound raised. The `sslCtxLiveCount` check is the real regression guard there — if that passes and LSAN is clean, raise the RSS bound."," - **`asn1_string_st` / `GENERAL_NAME_st` layout** — Bun mirrors these in `src/boringssl_sys/boringssl.rs`; diff `include/openssl/{asn1,x509v3}.h` for field changes.","+- **Values Rust hardcodes** — upstream has renumbered an enum (`ssl_compliance_policy_t`) and taken a flag bit the fork used (`X509_V_FLAG_*`). Neither fails to link. Diff macro values (`clang -dM -E`) and enums between the old and new `include/openssl`."],"additions":10,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/bun-usockets/src/node_quic_shim.c","lines":["@@ -188,6 +188,12 @@ static void nq_on_path_switch(lsquic_conn_t *c, int validated, int is_preferred,"," _Static_assert(sizeof(lsxpack_strlen_t) == 4 && offsetof(struct lsxpack_header, chain_next_idx) == sizeof(char *) + 24,","     \"LSXPACK_MAX_STRLEN must be UINT32_MAX\");"," ","+_Static_assert(ssl_compliance_policy_fips_202205 == 1 && ssl_compliance_policy_wpa3_192_202304 == 3 &&","+    ssl_early_data_unknown == 0 && ssl_early_data_disabled == 1 && ssl_early_data_no_session_offered == 5 &&","+    X509_V_FLAG_CRL_CHECK == 0x4 && X509_V_FLAG_CRL_CHECK_ALL == 0x8 &&","+    X509_V_FLAG_IGNORE_E